---
import SiteLayout from "../../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import Studio from "../../../components/Studio.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<SiteLayout title="CSS Studio — interactive design tokens" description="Try an accessible interactive CSS design-token lab: adjust color, radius, gap, columns and animation, then copy deterministic source CSS.">
  <div class="shell page-pad">
    <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href={base}>Lab home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span> CSS Studio</nav>
    <header class="inner-hero"><p class="eyebrow"><span class="status-led" aria-hidden="true"></span> LAB 001 / REAL INTERACTION</p><h1>CSS Studio<span class="heading-accent">.</span></h1><p>One small system. Five safe controls. The generated CSS is readable, reproducible, and yours to copy.</p></header>
    <Studio />
    <section class="below-studio" aria-labelledby="details"><div><p class="eyebrow">IMPLEMENTATION NOTES</p><h2 id="details">Inspect the decisions.</h2></div><div><p>All values come from a finite whitelist. No free-form CSS is interpreted, no user content is sent to a server, and the design works as a static page when JavaScript is disabled.</p><p>Keyboard focus is visible, reduced-motion preferences override animation, and copy failure exposes selectable text instead of pretending the clipboard worked.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/ruslanudintsev-ai/ruslan-ai-lab" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View the source repository ↗</a></div></section>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
